  "translation": {
    "literal": "The moon sets, a crow cries, and frost fills the sky; river maples and fishermen's lamps face me as I lie in sorrow. Outside the city of Gusu stands Cold Mountain Temple; its midnight bell reaches the traveller's boat.",
    "poetic": "The moon goes down, a crow calls, and frost fills the air. Maples on the shore and fishing lamps keep watch over my troubled sleep. Beyond the walls of Gusu stands Cold Mountain Temple, and its midnight bell tolls out to my boat."
  },
  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "place",
      "kind": "history",
      "title": "Maple Bridge and Cold Mountain Temple",
      "body": "Zhang Ji (c. 715 – c. 779) moored near the Maple Bridge (楓橋), a canal bridge outside Suzhou (姑蘇). The poem is usually dated to the years after the An Lushan Rebellion began (755), but the exact date is not certain. 寒山寺 is named after the monk Hanshan. The poem made both names famous across East Asia, and it has been carved on stone at the temple many times."
    },
    {
      "id": "bell",
      "kind": "interpretation",
      "title": "Does a temple ring at midnight?",
      "body": "The Song critic Ouyang Xiu objected that \"midnight is not the time to ring a bell\", but later scholars showed that Tang temples did ring at night, and the custom is recorded for Suzhou. The line shows how one sound, heard from a boat in the dark, can carry the whole poem."
    },
    {
      "id": "variants",
      "kind": "text-variant",
      "title": "Another reading of 江楓 and 愁眠",
      "body": "Some editions read 江村漁火 for 江楓漁火. Some scholars read 愁眠 as the name of a hill near Suzhou rather than \"sorrowful sleep\", and 江楓 as two bridges, 江村橋 and 楓橋. The simple reading taught in schools, the one used here, takes 愁眠 as the sleep of someone with a worried heart."
    },
    {
      "id": "rhyme",
      "kind": "rhyme",
      "title": "Rhyme: 天 · 眠 · 船",
      "body": "Lines one, two and four end in 天 (tiān), 眠 (mián) and 船 (chuán), in the 先 rhyme. Line three ends in 寺 and does not rhyme."
    }
  ],
